    "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:00:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:00:27Z",
    "body": "> > > [@theIDinside](https://github.com/theIDinside) do you want to submit a spec PR?\n> > \n> > \n> > Yeah I can fix that. I think the only concern I have beyond that is that users maybe expect that step to work?\n> \n> I don't think so. If you call redirect on a navigation that wasn't instantiated by the navigation API this should not be observable.\n> \n> The condition means that there is no call to do for a navigation API call because there wasn't one. It's the right thing.\n\nSorry, but just to be extra clear; the redirect call should still work, right? It's just that the serialize-portion of it, should not?",
